@format 1
@id section-modification.common.apply-modified-state
@title Apply modified section state
@section Section modification
@area Common
@entry apply-plan
@summary Apply an accepted modification, synchronously publish the changed section state, update Split visuals/history, save sidecar records, and then return to the operation-specific UI/logging continuation.
@related section-modification.set-start-on-selected-section, section-modification.set-end-on-selected-section, section-modification.toggle-section, section-modification.reorder-section-by-drag, section-modification.sort-sections
@tag section
@tag split
@tag modification
@tag persistence
@tag history

@alias segment = Cadroue.Application.LSegment
@alias flow = Cadroue.UIShell.PFlow.PFlow
@alias panel = Cadroue.UIShell.PPanels.PSection
@alias workspace = Cadroue.UIShell.PControlBar.PWorkspace
@alias history = Cadroue.Application.LHistory
@alias sidecar = Cadroue.Infrastructure.LSidecarStore

[apply-plan] Accepted existing-section modification <input>
= LSegmentStartSet, LSegmentEndSet, LSegmentDivide, LSegmentToggle, LSegmentMove, or LSegmentSort has produced a replacement section list and selection state.
> replace-state

[replace-state] Replace segment state <process>
- LSegmentApply replaces the internal pieces, sets the active index, and synchronously invokes LSegmentChange with a snapshot @ segment.LSegmentApply(...)
> flow-publish

[flow-publish] Publish the changed sections through Flow <process>
- PFlowSegmentHandle sets pFlowSegmentFired, updates Viewfinder and Map section geometry, then invokes PFlowSectionChange @ flow.PFlowSegmentHandle(...)
> panel-update

[panel-update] Sections-panel reaction <process>
- PSectionUpdateHandle stores the new list and selection; during live drag it intentionally returns without rebuilding, otherwise it rebuilds when section values/order changed or only reapplies selection when the list is unchanged @ panel.PSectionUpdateHandle(...)
> history-update

[history-update] Workspace undo-history reaction <process>
- PWorkspaceSectionHandle snapshots the workspace and asks LHistoryAdd to append it unless history is currently being applied or the state is already the current history entry @ workspace.PWorkspaceSectionHandle(...)
@ workspace.PWorkspaceHistoryAdd(...)
@ history.LHistoryAdd(...)
> sidecar-save

[sidecar-save] Save current section records <process>
- After LSegmentChange returns, LSegmentApply calls LSegmentSave; when a source path exists and restore mode is off, the configured seam attempts to write current section records to the media sidecar @ segment.LSegmentApply(...) / LSegmentSave after LSegmentChange
@ segment.LSegmentSave(...)
@ sidecar.LSidecarSectionsSave(...)
> caller-return

[caller-return] Resume originating modification <decision>
= Control returns synchronously through the originating LSegment call to its PFlow or panel caller.
? "Set Start" > start-log
? "Set End" > end-log
? "Split" > split-log
? "Toggle" > toggle-log
? "Move" > move-log
? "Sort" > sort-log

[start-log] Record changed start <output>
- LSegmentStartSet returns Added=false; PFlowStartSet records the selected section as start set @ flow.PFlowStartSet(...)
@ flow.PFlowSectionRecord(...)

[end-log] Record changed end <output>
- LSegmentEndSet returns Added=false; PFlowEndSet records the selected section as end set @ flow.PFlowEndSet(...)
@ flow.PFlowSectionRecord(...)

[split-log] Record split modification and creation <output>
- PFlowSectionDivide reads the selected left-half index after LSegmentDivide and records the shortened left half, then records the newly created right half; the creation-oriented view of this same operation is documented under Section creation @ flow.PFlowSectionDivide(...)
@ flow.PFlowSectionRecord(...)

[toggle-log] Record output-state toggle <output>
- PFlowSectionToggle sees the synchronous change, reads the indexed section's new LPieceHidden value, and records turned off when hidden or turned on when visible @ flow.PFlowSectionToggle(...)
@ flow.PFlowSectionRecord(...)

[move-log] Record move and update the live row <output>
- PFlowSectionMove records the final logical insertion and returns true; PSectionLiveMove then moves the dragged row to the same insertion index, updates its tracked drag index, and renumbers visible badges without a full rebuild during the drag @ flow.PFlowSectionMove(...)
@ flow.PFlowSectionRecord(...)
@ panel.PSectionLiveMove(...)
@ panel.PSectionNumberUpdate(...)

[sort-log] Record successful sort <output>
- PFlowSectionSort sees pFlowSegmentFired=true after the synchronous apply and records one Sections sorted by name information log @ flow.PFlowSectionSort(...)
